[? if left_split == 0 : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#940000'> </div> !}Left: {!</td><td>!} [+ lef_seats +]% ?]

[? if syn_created == 1 : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#913724'> </div> !}Syndycalists: {!</td><td>!} [+ syn_seats +]% ?]

[? if agrarnians_split == 0 : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#dd5b00'> </div> !}Agrarians: {!</td><td>!} [+ agr_seats +]% ?]

[? if centrists_resign == 0 : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#c96b65'> </div> !}Center: {!</td><td>!} [+ cen_seats +]% ?]

[? if unions_independent == 0 : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#c96b65'> </div> !}Labour: {!</td><td>!} [+ lab_seats +]% ?]

[? if reformists_resigned == 0 : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#dc0200'> </div> !}Refrormist: {!</td><td>!} [+ ref_seats +]% ?]

{!</table>!}

-@congress_begin_2: Let the Congress Begin...

# BEGIN - REFORM OR REVOLUTION  --------------------------------------------------


@congress_begin_2

= Main issue Reform or Revolution 

The classic question of every <span style="color: #d61818;">Socialist</span> is **Reform Or Revolution**

Should we focus our actions on <span style="color: #b50000;">Revolutionary</span> means and the preparation of the People's Revolution?

Or shoud we focus on Parlimtary, <span style="color: #dc0200;">Reformist</span> ways and try to get into the Federal Goverment?

-@full_rev: The party is fully centered on Revolutionary action. 
-@part_rev: We are focusing on revolutionary action, but we still remain commited to parlimentary means. 
-@part_ref: We are focusing on parlimentary action, but we still remain commited to revolutionary means. 
-@full_ref: The party is fully centered on Reformist and Parlimentary action.

@full_rev
choose-if: (rev_seats + lef_seats) > (ref_seats + cen_seats)
on-arrival: party_policy_main = 3; revolutionaries_dissent -= 10; left_dissent -= 8; center_dissent += 8; labor_dissent += 16; reformist_dissent += 50; radicalization += 2; democratization -= 2; pacifism -= 1;

We decided to fully support the <span style="color: #b50000;">Revolution</span>.

This is a shocking move and this mean essentialy the end of the United Party, as we can now essentialy expect the <span style="color: #dc0200;">SPM</span> to split form the party...

-@revolution: Continue to the congress

@part_rev
on-arrival: party_policy_main = 2; revolutionaries_dissent -= 4; left_dissent -= 2; agrarnians_dissent -= 2; labor_dissent += 4; reformist_dissent += 8; radicalization += 1; democratization -= 1;

Our policy of focusing on the <span style="color: #b50000;">Revolutionary</span> means while continously supporting the <span style="color: #dc0200;">Reformist</span> ways. 

This can balance party wings, but it sets the policy to work towars a revolution. 

-@revolution: Continue to the congress

@part_ref
on-arrival: party_policy_main = 1; revolutionaries_dissent += 6; left_dissent += 4; center_dissent -= 6; labor_dissent -= 4; reformist_dissent -= 4; radicalization -= 1; democratization += 1;

Our policy of focusing on the <span style="color: #dc0200;">Reformist</span> means while continously supporting the <span style="color: #b50000;">Revolutionary</span> ways. 

This can balance party wings, but it sets the policy to work towars a parlimentary participation. 

-@revolution: Continue to the congress

@full_ref
choose-if: (ref_seats + cen_seats/2) > (rev_seats + lef_seats + lab_seats/2 + agr_seats/2)
on-arrival: party_policy_main = 0; revolutionaries_dissent += 50; left_dissent += 14; agrarnians_dissent += 2; center_dissent += 2; reformist_dissent -= 10; radicalization -= 2; democratization += 2; pacifism += 1;

We decided to fully support the <span style="color: #dc0200;">Reformist</span> way of parlimentary participation.

This is a shocking move and this mean essentialy the end of the United Party, as we can now essentialy expect the <span style="color: #b50000;">KPM</span> to split form the party...

-@revolution: Continue to the congress

#  revolution ---------------------------------------------------

@revolution

= Issue of Revolution 

Now that we have pushed for <span style="color: #b50000;">Revolutionary</span> means to be endorced by the party, we need to decide our policy towards the <span style="color: #b50000;">Revolution</span> itself. 

We have consistenty supported moderate buildup of <span style="color: #b50000;">Revolutionary</span> forces, while not focusing on them esspecialy. But this congress might change it. 

-@immi: We should strive for the revolution as soon as possible!
-@build: We must build up and wait for the good moment for our revolution, but dont start it now.
-@down: Our revolutionary preparations should be toned down a bit in a list of party priorities, but we stand commited to the revolutionary struggle. 
-@nutral: We do not condemn revolutionary action but nidher we do support it.
-@condem: Condemn any revolutionary acions. 

@immi
choose-if: ((rev_seats + lef_seats) > (ref_seats + cen_seats)) and party_policy_main > 1
on-arrival: party_policy_rev = 3; revolutionaries_dissent -= 10; left_dissent -= 8; agrarnians_dissent -= 4; center_dissent += 4; labor_dissent += 4; reformist_dissent += 20; liberal_reconciliation -= 4; liberal_unity += 5; radicalization += 2; pacifism -= 2;

**RISE UP ALL VICTIMS OF OPPRESION**

We will call for the immedete revoltion and focus our reusocrces on preparing it and launch in as soon as possible.

-@coaltions: Continue the congress

@build
choose-if: party_policy_main > 1
on-arrival: party_policy_rev = 2; revolutionaries_dissent -= 8; left_dissent -= 6; agrarnians_dissent -= 2; reformist_dissent += 8; radicalization += 1;

This is a moderate <span style="color: #c96b65;">Center Marxist</span> position, as most of the party support the broader <span style="color: #b50000;">Revolution</span>.
It should apease the <span style="color: #b50000;">Revolutionatries</span>, while not alienating the <span style="color: #dc0200;">Reformists</span>

-@coaltions: Continue to the congress

@condem
view-if: party_policy_main = 0
on-arrival: party_policy_rev = -1; revolutionaries_dissent += 20; left_dissent += 10; agrarnians_dissent += 6; center_dissent += 6; reformist_dissent -= 10; liberal_reconciliation += 3; liberal_unity -= 3; radicalization -= 2; pacifism += 2;

This is a radical opinio and now many expet of the hardline <span style="color: #dc0200;">Reformists</span> support it, but it might give us a immence help in colaborating with the burgoise.

-@coaltions: Continue to the congress

@down
choose-if: party_policy_main >= 0 and party_policy_main <= 2
on-arrival: party_policy_rev = 1; revolutionaries_dissent += 8; left_dissent += 5; agrarnians_dissent += 3; reformist_dissent -= 6; 

This is a moderate <span style="color: #c96b65;">Center Marxist</span> position, as most of the party support the broader <span style="color: #b50000;">Revolution</span>, but in moderation.
It should apease the <span style="color: #dc0200;">Reformists</span>, while not alienating the <span style="color: #b50000;">Revolutionatries</span>

-@coaltions: Continue to the congress

@nutral
choose-if: ((rev_seats + lef_seats) < (ref_seats + cen_seats/2)) and party_policy_main < 2
on-arrival: party_policy_rev = 0; revolutionaries_dissent += 14; left_dissent += 7; agrarnians_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 4; center_dissent += 4; reformist_dissent -= 8; radicalization -= 1;

This policy might wash our hands from the <span style="color: #b50000;">Revolutionary</span> violence, but it will strongly alienate the factions supporting it. 

-@coaltions: Continue to the congress

# COALITION ---------------------------------------------------

@coaltions

= The issue of palimentary coalitions 

Now that we have pushed for parlimentary actions to be endorced by the party, we need to decide our policy towards the coalitionmaking and how much we are willing to compromise in order to enter the goverment.

The <span style="color: #d61818;">Socialist Majorty</span> policy was our position since the creation of our party, and serves as the main point of the united party. 

But with the possible changes in the political landscape, we might alter our policy. 

-@soc_maj: We should strive to achieve a socialist majorty and do not compromise with the burgoise.
-@zel: Our parlimetary efforts should strive to rebuild our links with the left wing liberals to potentilay enter a goverment with us, that would not require us to beray our ideas. 
-@libe: We should be fully open to any and all coalitons, even if it means compomising our more radlical goals. 

@soc_maj
choose-if: ((rev_seats + lef_seats) > ref_seats) and party_policy_main < 3
on-arrival: party_policy_coalition = 2; revolutionaries_dissent -= 6; left_dissent -= 6; agrarnians_dissent += 6; labor_dissent += 6; center_dissent += 2; reformist_dissent += 8;

The <span style="color: #d61818;">Socialist Majorty</span> was our go to option keeping the party united and we will continue to stand by it.

-@union: Continue the congress

@zel
choose-if: party_policy_main < 3
on-arrival: party_policy_coalition = 1; revolutionaries_dissent += 4; left_dissent += 4; agrarnians_dissent -= 2; labor_dissent -= 4; center_dissent -= 4; reformist_dissent -= 4; liberal_reconciliation += 1; democratization += 2;

This in a pragmatic option as it would be much easier to enter the goverment with the {!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Progressive People's Party" style="color: #ddd500;">FVP</span>!} or {!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Gecherdist Democratic Social Union" style="color: #48b94a;">GDSU</span>!} rather than alone. 

-@union: Continue to the congress

@libe
choose-if: ((rev_seats + lef_seats) < (ref_seats + cen_seats/2)) and party_policy_main < 2
on-arrival: party_policy_coalition = 0; revolutionaries_dissent += 10; left_dissent += 6; agrarnians_dissent += 4; labor_dissent += 2; center_dissent += 6; reformist_dissent -= 10; liberal_reconciliation += 3; liberal_unity -= 3; democratization += 3;

This is the most hardline <span style="color: #dc0200;">Reformists</span> position and it is not supported buy most of the wings of the party, but this will certainly work to break the <span style="color: #ccc912;">Liberal</span> alliance against us. 

-@union: Continue to the congress

# UNIONS ---------------------------------------------

@union

= Issue of trade unions

Next issue on the party congress list is the status of the unions. 

<span style="color: #c96b65;">Labour Unions</span> play a vital role in our economy, life and the party. What should be our policy towards them? 

-@party: Unions should be closer suborinated to the party.
-@quo: Maintain the current policy of "ideological lead by the party and operational indepence of the union".
-@independent: The unions should retain its relative independence form the party to most efficently expand their membership. 
-@syn: The party should be subordinated to the unions and to the direct will of the people. 

@party
choose-if: (cen_seats/2 + lef_seats/2 + ref_seats/2) > (rev_seats/2 + lab_seats)
on-arrival: party_policy_unions = 3; revolutionaries_dissent -= 2; left_dissent -= 4; labor_dissent += 10; center_dissent -= 6; reformist_dissent -= 4; syn_support -= 2;

This option allows us to try to forcefully integrate some of the Independent unions, but it makes them also more phrone to rebel agains the party if we dissapoint them.

<span style="color: #c96b65;">Labour</span> faction dislikes this decision. 

-@para: Continue the congress

@quo
on-arrival: party_policy_unions = 2; labor_dissent += 2; center_dissent -= 2; reformist_dissent -= 2; union_spd -= 10; union_lef_id += 10;

Maintaining the status current policy is widely supported across the party. It allows the relative freedom of the Unions and states that they shall support the party ideologically.

-@para: Continue to the congress

@independent
choose-if: (rev_seats/2 + lab_seats) > (ref_seats/2 + cen_seats/2 + lef_seats/2)
on-arrival: party_policy_unions = 1; revolutionaries_dissent += 4; left_dissent += 4; labor_dissent -= 8; center_dissent += 2; syn_support += 1; union_spd += 4; union_lef_id += 12; organisation_workers += 1;

Giving the unions more independence allows them to operate more freely and attract more members, but loosens the party grip over them and may result in them slipping away from us. 

-@para: Continue to the congress

@syn
choose-if: (rev_seats + lab_seats) > (ref_seats + cen_seats + lef_seats/2 + agr_seats/2)
on-arrival: party_policy_unions = 0; revolutionaries_dissent -= 8; left_dissent -= 6; labor_dissent -= 14; center_dissent += 6; reformist_dissent += 10;

syn

-@para: Continue to the congress

# PARAMILTARIES ---------------------------------------------

@para

congress start

= Issue of the Paramilitraies

-@revolution_usage: Our Paramilitaries priority is to work towards preparing the revolution.
-@party_defevce: The primary duty of our forces should be to defend the party and support it.
-@fight_right: The paramilitaries should focus of fignting and egtting rid of the reactionary forces. 
-@republic: Commit the paramiltaries to defend the Federation agains the threats from the reactionares. 

@revolution_usage
choose-if: ((rev_seats + lef_seats) > (ref_seats + cen_seats)) and party_policy_main > 1
